+# TB-SEC-KEY-01-R1 — isolated local PAPER dashboard authentication
+
+Scope: repair the shared-UID credential-file exposure reported in TB-SEC-KEY-01. Qualification deployment only; no live trading, real exchange credentials, wallet secrets, remote TLS or exchange authorization. Preserve the financial, independent recovery and native execution authority boundaries. The dashboard is not a venue adapter.
+
+## Architecture and reviewed migration
+
+- The original `maj-vaj-paper-dashboard.service` is now the **authentication gateway**, a loopback-only HTTP listener on 8765 under a dedicated non-login `maj-vaj-dashboard-auth` identity and its exclusive group. Its only systemd-loaded credential is the dashboard bearer. It has no access to the desk DB, vault, key source directory, signing or approval stores. Process memory protection and core limits remain. It has no arbitrary outbound destination or proxy environment; only a fixed Unix transport. No token, cookies, forwarded identity, origin or request trace reaches the backend. Exact public asset paths are the only unauthenticated forwarding exception. Canonical paths, host/origin, bounded requests/responses, fixed errors, no redirects, no-store and existing browser security headers are enforced.
+- `maj-vaj-dashboard-backend.socket` is root-created and root-owned, mode 0660, group `maj-vaj-dashboard-auth`, in a root-owned non-writable directory. `maj-vaj-paper-dashboard-backend.service` receives only that named systemd listening FD; no public or loopback TCP fallback, no bearer/key mounts, source-level refusal of credential environment variables. The private backend refuses forwarded Authorization headers. Ordinary desk/public-data UIDs cannot connect to the socket. The dedicated gateway UID is the trusted caller by design; root and that trusted service identity are not protected from themselves. The shared desk UID still trusts its own DB and backend operations; this change does not assert isolation from a compromised desk or privileged host. No remote network authentication is provided.
+- Reviewed cold migration only: stop old qualification dashboard and backend, remove obsolete standalone TCP processes, create a unique system user and group for the auth role (no other primary or supplemental members), deploy root-owned source and all three unit files plus existing vault, verify credentials are root-owned in `/etc/maj-vaj/credential-keys`, and verify unit dependencies. The opt-in markers remain required. Do not place actual secrets in the qualification dashboard. `scripts/qualify_dashboard_auth_guest_setup.sh` is a disposable OFFLINE guest-only bootstrap, not a production installer. `scripts/qualify_dashboard_auth_custody.py` is its synthetic installed acceptance harness. The old credential qualification setup and matrix are adapted to the separate service layout.
+- Public-data workers retain the desk UID and allowlisted subprocess environment. The gateway runs no workers. Existing research export is a verified, frozen market-only handoff, without features/labels/training or trading permission. It is not a live Cognitum connection.
+
+## Evidence and qualification boundaries
+
+Attach final evidence and distinguish any unexecuted installed test. No credentials or test secret values in reports. The actual browser persistence, notification/support/debug surfaces, network egress matrix, provider scope verification/revocation and key-encryption-key rotation/operator-approved encrypted restore remain separate production release gates. Local credential removal is not remote provider revocation. Loopback HTTP qualification is not production TLS readiness.
+
+### Executed qualification, 2026-11-20
+
+- Verified the previous candidate ZIP, patch and evidence SHA256 manifest. Imported the recovered source snapshot locally; the resulting local Git ancestry is not represented as the original upstream history. Verified the pinned offline Python 3.12.16/Freqtrade 2026.10 wheelhouse, `pip check` clean. Six new gateway regressions PASS. Headless full suite initially failed two pre-existing graphical tests for an unavailable display; repeat under Xvfb: 527 discovered, 525 passed, two optional skips, zero failures, 53.994s. This full run preceded the final exclusive-group preflight refinement; focused tests and the installed runtime matrix cover the final change.
+- Actual Debian 13 systemd guest (QEMU software emulation, no NIC; loopback only): eight original VM inputs and all 15 QEMU dependency-manifest entries matched. Fresh child disk. Offline dependency install PASS, opt-in marker refusals and named service startup PASS. The first final-source readiness attempt used a fixed 5s delay and failed before the auth listener became ready; the backend was inactive until socket activation. A bounded HTTP readiness retry then passed without changing production settings. No secret-bearing diagnostics included.
+- Final installed audit exit 0, all 15 checkpoints PASS. Distinct named gateway/backend/vault identities; desk and four other untrusted service identities denied bearer file, auth memory and direct private socket; gateway denied desk and vault files; valid HTTP authorization and forbidden web enrollment; synthetic local enrollment, paired replacement, partial removal refusal, restart persistence; actual root-controlled replacement of synthetic dashboard token with gateway restart (previous token refused, replacement accepted). Actual dashboard-initiated market-only backup completed while the synthetic credentials were stored. Observed the real public-data child process and verified its environment and argv were free of synthetic marker forms and credential variables. Exported and verified the actual frozen market-only research handoff under the desk role from two controlled synthetic hourly data observations; no training or execution authority. Scanned stored desk/vault/backup/handoff files, observed worker, process args/environment and journals for raw/hex/base64 enrolled marker forms and both old/new synthetic bearer markers and KEK. No canaries observed in these checked surfaces; local credential removal passed. No live venue access or real funds, no Cognitum data transmission. This is not exhaustive non-disclosure or remote key revocation.
+- All 109 final top-level runtime Python files and deployment definitions matched the installed source manifest; stopped all four named service/socket units, verified private sockets and credential mounts retired. Graceful poweroff, child `qemu-img check` no errors; base SHA256 unchanged `2eba10bdfc7f368dde145205e0f3211f5f3a0ce29a5ab60b5ea7b728fd9a1776`. No CI or GitHub mainline changes.
+
+**Disposition:** R1 isolated dashboard custody, scoped installed worker/market-only handoff and synthetic local credential replacement/removal and bearer restart rotation PASS. Parent TB-SEC-KEY-01 remains OPEN for actual browser persistence and outbound/notification/support surfaces, independent venue adapter and positive key scope verification, provider-side revocation, KEK rotation and operator-approved encrypted recovery, remote TLS, and consolidated installed acceptance. No production or live authorization.
